      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $631$\n\nII. $782$\n\nIII. $686$",
      "worked_solution": "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $631,$ we have that \n\n$$\n63-2(1)=63-2=61\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $631$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $782,$ we have that \n\n$$\n78-2(2)=78-4=74\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $782$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $686,$ we have that \n\n$$\n68-2(6)=68-12=56\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $686$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
